{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\nA misleading error code is a significant failure mode: it causes LLM/agent consumers to make erroneous assumptions and act on a wrong diagnosis (e.g. \"the AI provider is down\" when the real fault is bad input or a missing asset). Recent bugs are all instances of ONE systemic pattern: the blanket `LLMError -> llm_unavailable` fallthrough in the workflow `error_code_for` classifier mislabels non-LLM failures.\n\nKnown instances: 35ab (unknown-step -> llm_unavailable, FIXED -> invalid_input), 551b (missing-bundle -> llm_unavailable, DEFERRED/latent), 73d8 (ExpressionError -> llm_unavailable, pending design decision).\n\n## Goal\nSystematically audit EVERY error-code / classification surface so each returned code accurately and specifically describes the actual condition, and no failure degrades to a misleading catch-all.\n\n## Unified principle (resolved)\nReserve the error code `llm_unavailable` for genuine availability faults ONLY — `isinstance(exc, LLMUnavailableError)` including `LLMConfigError`. Route every other `LLMError` subclass to the existing broad-but-accurate `command_failed`. Discriminate by exception TYPE, not by phase. Do NOT invent new fine-grained error codes on the workflow vocabulary.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `error_code_for` (src/rebar/_errors.py) maps only `LLMUnavailableError` (incl. `LLMConfigError`) to `llm_unavailable`; every other `LLMError` subclass maps to `command_failed` (child f75f-5509-10c0-4430).\n- [ ] `_structured_llm_failure` (src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py) derives its top-level `error` field via `error_code_for(exc)` instead of hardcoding `llm_unavailable`, across all 4 MCP gate tools (child fbc0-ee15-9d69-49ae).\n- [ ] The `render_workflow` MCP tool surfaces the `WorkflowError` family as `command_failed` (not `llm_unavailable`), proven by an observable test asserting through the tool's error envelope (child 7d47-2131-42bd-4832).\n- [ ] `pinned_ticket_read_failed` is registered in `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` (child 0aee-a70d-045b-48a1).\n- [ ] The gate-degrade `coverage.llm_unavailable` boolean is True only for genuine `LLMUnavailableError` outages; `LLMInputRejectedError` instead sets a distinct `input_rejected` signal, and the three readers (`plan_review/drift_floor.py`, `plan_review/orchestrator.py`, `review_bot/adapter.py`) are updated to read it (child 5f96-25aa-af9d-4f57).\n- [ ] A prevention guardrail lands: an exhaustive `exception → code` contract test over `LLMError.__subclasses__()` asserting each subclass maps to its intended code by type, plus a vocabulary-closure test asserting every code any producer can emit is in `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES`.\n- [ ] Every change lands via Gerrit with `Verified +1` and `LLM-Review +1`, carries a `rebar-ticket` trailer + DCO sign-off, and children are closed bottom-up.\n\n## Scope (surfaces enumerated by the audit)\n- Workflow error-code vocabulary + `error_code_for` mapping (`src/rebar/_errors.py`) — esp. the blanket `LLMError -> llm_unavailable` fallthrough branch.\n- `_structured_llm_failure` (`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py`) across the 4 MCP gate tools.\n- The gate-degrade `coverage.llm_unavailable` boolean (`gate_dispatch.py` / `plan_review_recovery.py`) and its three readers.\n- Top-level `_errors.py` `KNOWN_ERROR_CODES` vocabulary contract.\n\n## Constraints\nRemediation lands via Gerrit per AGENTS.md. No --force. Gates run unbounded. 73d8 and 551b linked in as instances of this epic; both are resolved by the type-discriminated `error_code_for` narrowing (a genuine execute-time outage is an `LLMUnavailableError` and stays `llm_unavailable`; an `ExpressionError`/WorkflowError is not → `command_failed`)."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788060854118234892,"uuid":"1614e3a0-ef36-41b2-90fe-6411fb12724b"}